    "updated_at": "2016-07-08T11:38:44Z",
    "body": "> (Also, they only want to apply their hooks to the top-level fetches.)\n\nThis is true. All the error handling in the custom perform the fetch in SW update is only for the top-level fetch.\n\n> in that issue, but I don't see how that makes sense. @jungkees @jakearchibald, surely service workers need to cache the entire module script tree?\n\n**This is also true.** Unless we cache the entire module script tree, the SW script will fail when offline. @domenic, I just want to double check if I understand it right - When \"Fetch a module worker script tree\" algorithm asynchronously completes with a module script, that module script is the final script that can be evaluated through \"run the module script\"? If that's right, everything looks fine as we store the result module script to the service worker's script resource for later runs.\n",
