    "created_at": "2016-07-08T18:41:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-08T18:41:41Z",
    "body": "> When \"Fetch a module worker script tree\" algorithm asynchronously completes with a module script, that module script is the final script that can be evaluated through \"run the module script\"?\n\nYes. But... it's only one module script. The rest of the module scripts in the tree (i.e. those `import`ed through ES6 syntax) are seperate module maps. Is that OK? Maybe it should also hook non-top-level fetches and store them in the script resource map? (I don't understand the purpose of the script resource map; it seems like it's a duplicate of the HTTP cache specifically for `importScripts` that only varies on request URL.)\n",
